But nethack is a multigoal game. Minetown and protection (if you choose to
take it on) is only one of at least a dozen subgoals that must be conquered
before ascending. You've mastered the first one. You need to start working
on the second or the third. Sokoban is usually my second target. Securing
Magic Resistance is the third. Mines End is the fourth. There are many more.

First and foremost you have to work at slowing down. You were right on point
that it's carelessness that's your ultimate enemy. Just like the rules for
the protection run, you'll need to create some rules for yourself so that
you can consistently achieve the next goal.

My current goal that I'm working on is kicking Master Kaen's ass consistently
without getting killed in the process. I got him once. He's gotten me about
5 or 6 times. I'll keep working on it until either I can do it consistently
or until I ascend the monk class and move on to the next (probably a priest).

